# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` with no exclusions otherwise — without this
# file, a build bakes in whatever happens to be in data/ (SQLite DB, inbox
# files) and, worse, config/leg_config.yaml (which can hold real MQTT/IMAP
# credentials, see README) as an image layer. Both are bind-mounted at
# runtime anyway (see docker-compose.yml), so none of this is needed in the
# image itself.

data/
config/leg_config.yaml

.git/
.github/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
tests/
docs/
ha_addon/
